Might require fewer API changes in the end. Would probably be S4, but S3 equivalent looks like this:

```
Query <- function(sql, params = NULL) {
  structure(list(sql=sql, params=params), class = "Query")
}

c.Query <- function(...) {
  queries <- list(...)
  zipped <- purrr::zip_n(queries)
  structure(
    list(sql = paste(zipped$sql, collapse = "\n"),
         params = unlist(zipped$params, recursive = FALSE)),
    class = "Query")
}
```

The `c()` makes it much easier to combine queries with parameters. ~~Only works with positional placeholders, though -- need to add support for ?-style placeholders to Postgres (via `sqlInterpolate()`).~~

e.g.

``` R
setMethod("dbGetQuery", signature("MyConnection", "character"),
  function(conn, statement, ..., params = NULL, row.names = NA) {
    rs <- dbSendQuery(conn, statement, params = params, ...)
    on.exit(dbClearResult(rs))

    dbFetch(rs, n = -1, ..., row.names = row.names)
  }
)
```
